  "operation": {
    "kind": "prompt",
    "user": "Establish this phase's working set, and answer the one question that decides whether an\nexploration runs.\n\nYou are the context state for the **{{.inputs.phase}}** phase.\n\n## The standing docs\n\n{{.inputs.standing}}\n\nThese paths are constants — §0.4 names them, and they do not change between features.\n\n## The catalog\n\n{{.inputs.catalog}}\n\nA path, like the standing docs. Open it with `read_file`.\n\n## What this phase has been asked to serve\n\n{{.inputs.subject}}\n\n## What to do\n\n**Read the catalog, and the standing docs.** Use `read_file`. Read the catalog *index*\nfirst — it is the table, and it is what tells you what exists without opening\neverything — then open only the entries that could plausibly bear on the subject.\n\n**Answer the match question.** This is the judgment this state exists for, and the only\npart of it a machine could not do:\n\n> Does something in the catalog already cover this, well enough that building a new one\n> would be duplication?\n\nBe honest in both directions. A false yes sends the phase to draft against a doc that\ndoes not fit, and the mismatch surfaces three phases later as a component nobody can\nuse. A false no spends a whole exploration re-deriving a decision that is already\nwritten down — and §0.5 is explicit that \"an exploration when an existing pattern fits\nis waste\".\n\nWhere the answer is yes, **name what matched and why**, so the draft state can\ninstantiate it rather than guessing what you meant.\n\n**Report the working set as PATHS, not contents.** Which docs bear on this feature —\nthe standing docs, the catalog entries that matched or nearly did, and anything the\nsubject depends on. The states after you have `read_file` too; handing them paths means\nthey read the file as it is now, rather than a copy taken before this phase started\nediting.\n\n## What to produce\n\n`matched` — a boolean: does the catalog already cover this?\n\n`match_reason` — one or two sentences. On a yes, what matched and why it fits. On a no,\nwhat you checked and why the nearest entry does not fit. A bare `false` with nothing\nbehind it is the answer that gets rubber-stamped.\n\n`working_set` — the paths, each with one line saying why it is in the set.\n\n`near_matches` — the catalog entries you considered and rejected, with their paths. The\ndraft state is required to record what it checked before building, and this is that\nrecord.\n",
    "config": {
      "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5"
    },
    "input": {},
    "output": {
      "name": "output",
      "kind": "json",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "matched": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "match_reason": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "working_set": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "near_matches": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "matched",
          "match_reason",
          "working_set",
          "near_matches"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "environment": {
    "tools": [
      "read_file"
    ]
  },
  "slotMeta": {
    "inputs.phase": {
      "default": "product"
    },
    "inputs.standing": {
      "default": [
        "docs/product/principles.md"
      ],
      "description": "The standing docs §0.4 gives this phase. Constants — nothing computes them."
    },
    "inputs.catalog": {
      "default": [
        "docs/product/index.md"
      ],
      "description": "This area's catalog index. A constant — nothing computes it."
    },
    "inputs.subject": {
      "optional": true,
      "description": "What this phase has been asked to serve — the issue, or the upstream phase's output."
    }
  }
